Attention of an image with itself may take its keys and values from a coarser grid

A SpatialTransformer lays its image of w by h out as w h tokens, row after row, and its blocks run with the grid recorded in the runner's context (token_width, token_height). With SD_USE_SDASM defined, as stable-diffusion.assembly defines it for the library, a CrossAttention of the tokens with themselves asks stable-diffusion.assembly by how much to coarsen the grid (sdasm_token_downsampling(), which the run's SDASM_TUNE=todo=2 or 3 sets, for grids of todo_tokens tokens or more): by more than 1, its keys and values are those of the tokens at every factor-th column of every factor-th row, the token nearest each point of the coarser grid, and its queries every token -- ToDo (Smith, Saxena and Saha, Token Downsampling for Efficient Generation of High-Resolution Images, IJCAI 2024), which takes the keys and values by nearest-neighbour downsampling. The coarse tokens are taken before the keys' and the values' projections, which then project a factor squared fewer of them. Without SD_USE_SDASM, or by 1, attention is as it was.

The block includes stable-diffusion.assembly's header (sources/sdasm.h), which the project gives the library, so that the compiler holds the call to the function's declaration.

This is stable-diffusion.assembly's own patch, applied to the submodule by cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, after patch 0003; it is not for upstream. stable-diffusion.cpp's part is under the MIT License, and the patch's under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version.

